        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "71db7029-8503-574e-be6e-962d3a7af16c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Charcoal Tank Nature Reserve, West Wyalong, New South Wales, Australia\n- Systems: Newell Highway, Mid-Western Highway, The Charcoal Tank Road\n- Organizations: Bland Shire\n- Topics: protected areas, location, transport access\n\nFacts:\n- Charcoal Tank Nature Reserve is a protected nature reserve in the central western region of New South Wales, Australia.\n- Charcoal Tank Nature Reserve covers 86.4 hectares.\n- Charcoal Tank Nature Reserve is located 10 km south of West Wyalong.\n- Charcoal Tank Nature Reserve can be accessed via the Newell Highway and The Charcoal Tank Road.\n- West Wyalong is a town in New South Wales, Australia.\n- West Wyalong is the main town of Bland Shire.\n- West Wyalong is in the Central West region of New South Wales.\n- West Wyalong is at the crossroads of the Newell Highway and the Mid-Western Highway.\n- The Newell Highway route at West Wyalong connects Melbourne and Brisbane.\n- The Mid-Western Highway route at West Wyalong connects Sydney and Adelaide.",
